Balances, reservations, counters.

368
00:33:20.653 --> 00:33:21.890
Store (reference):

369
00:33:22.170 --> 00:33:29.295
In-memory partitioned store with synchronous replicas (commercial OCS or in-memory data grid or purpose-built).

370
00:33:29.575 --> 00:33:30.386
Notes:

371
00:33:30.666 --> 00:33:33.717
Millions TPS; single writer per partition.

372
00:33:33.997 --> 00:33:34.850
Catalogue.

373
00:33:35.130 --> 00:33:36.367
Store (reference):

374
00:33:36.647 --> 00:33:41.383
Versioned catalogue database; compiled artefacts pushed to OCS and billing.

375
00:33:41.663 --> 00:33:42.474
Notes:

376
00:33:42.754 --> 00:33:45.037
TM Forum SID-based model.

377
00:33:45.317 --> 00:33:47.109
Customers, accounts, orders.

378
00:33:47.389 --> 00:33:48.626
Store (reference):

379
00:33:48.906 --> 00:33:50.314
Relational (sharded).

380
00:33:50.594 --> 00:33:51.405
Notes:

381
00:33:51.685 --> 00:33:53.669
CRM and order management.

382
00:33:53.949 --> 00:33:55.741
Subscriber network profiles.

383
00:33:56.021 --> 00:33:57.258
Store (reference):

384
00:33:57.538 --> 00:34:00.055
HSS or UDM (network side).

385
00:34:00.335 --> 00:34:01.146
Notes:

386
00:34:01.426 --> 00:34:02.919
Provisioned by BSS.

387
00:34:03.199 --> 00:34:04.842
Postpaid bills and payments.

388
00:34:05.122 --> 00:34:06.359
Store (reference):

389
00:34:06.639 --> 00:34:09.306
Relational + document store for invoices.

390
00:34:09.586 --> 00:34:10.397
Notes:

391
00:34:10.677 --> 00:34:11.893
Retained per rules.

392
00:34:13.243 --> 00:34:14.373
Usage records.

393
00:34:14.653 --> 00:34:15.891
Store (reference):

394
00:34:16.171 --> 00:34:19.307
Raw files or streams, then lake (compressed columnar).

395
00:34:19.587 --> 00:34:20.397
Notes:

396
00:34:20.677 --> 00:34:22.213
Tens of billions per day.

397
00:34:22.493 --> 00:34:24.179
Number inventory, porting.

398
00:34:24.459 --> 00:34:25.696
Store (reference):

399
00:34:25.976 --> 00:34:26.872
Relational.

400
00:34:27.152 --> 00:34:27.963
Notes:

401
00:34:28.243 --> 00:34:29.544
MNP workflows.

402
00:34:30.894 --> 00:34:32.771
Usage data pipeline and lake.

403
00:34:33.051 --> 00:34:44.166
Volume: tens of billions of records per day, that is, hundreds of thousands to millions of records per second, at ~200 to 500 bytes each before compression.

404
00:34:44.446 --> 00:34:46.665
That is several TB per day compressed.

405
00:34:46.945 --> 00:35:05.825
Pipeline: mediation, then Kafka (partitioned by subscriber), then streaming processors (Flink) for real-time features (fraud, usage notifications, network analytics), then lake in columnar formats (Parquet or ORC in Iceberg or Hudi tables), partitioned by date and hour.

406
00:35:07.175 --> 00:35:07.943
Query:

407
00:35:08.223 --> 00:35:18.335
Spark for heavy jobs, Trino or Presto or ClickHouse for interactive analysis, pre-aggregated marts (usage per subscriber per day, per cell per hour).

408
00:35:18.615 --> 00:35:28.833
Retention: raw usage records kept for the period required by licence conditions (VERIFY), with secure, access-controlled archives for lawful requests.

409
00:35:30.183 --> 00:35:31.698
Warehouse and analytics.

410
00:35:31.978 --> 00:35:45.055
Subject areas: subscribers and plans; recharges and revenue; usage (daily aggregates); network quality per cell; churn and port-outs; campaigns; interconnect and roaming; fraud cases.

411
00:35:45.335 --> 00:35:46.317
Key metrics:

412
00:35:46.597 --> 00:35:53.039
ARPU (average revenue per user);. data usage per subscriber;. recharge frequency;. churn rate;.

413
00:35:54.389 --> 00:35:58.357
revenue leakage;. network quality correlated with churn by area.

414
00:35:58.637 --> 00:36:08.643
Regulatory reporting: subscriber counts and activity reports, tariff filings and quality of service reports to the regulator (VERIFY required returns).

415
00:36:09.993 --> 00:36:10.974
Data flow.

416
00:36:11.254 --> 00:36:12.598
